tirely, removed the authored thread from the trending list, reverted thread-1's upvote count back to 47, and reset community stats.threads back to the original 1,045. No registered accounts, profile edits, discussions, replies, or votes survive a reload.\", \"evidence\": \"Pre-reload: signed in as ft13tester, thread-1 upvotes=48, stats.threads presumably 1,046 with new thread included. Post-reload snapshot: navigation shows Login/Register (logged out), thread-1.upvotes=47, stats.threads=1,045, authored thread absent from list.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Submitting entirely blank form showed toast 'Please fill in all fields' and no thread created. Submitting with title+body filled but category unselected also blocked with same message, remained on /new-thread with entered values preserved, confirming no discussion created without category.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Incorrect password is accepted and creates a logged-in session\", \"actual\": \"After logging out of qatester01, submitted login with correct email but wrong password ('wrongpassword'). The app redirected to home page and showed the user as fully signed in (nav.profile = 'qatester01', logout button present), instead of rejecting the credentials.\", \"evidence\": \"Post-submit snapshot: navigation includes nav.profile 'qatester01' and action nav.logout, confirming an authenticated session was created with wrong password.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No in-app entry point to start a discussion while logged out, and direct navigation to the discussion-creation route renders a blank page instead of a sign-in screen\", \"actual\": \"While logged out, the home page navigation only shows Login/Register (no 'New Thread'/'Start Discussion' link), so there is no in-app way to attempt starting a discussion. Directly visiting /new-thread (reproduced twice) renders a completely blank page (only an empty notifications region) with no sign-in form and no redirect to /login.\", \"evidence\": \"browser_snapshot on /new-thread while logged out (reproduced): only '- generic [active]: - generic: - region \\\"Notifications alt+T\\\"'.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Trending list initially ordered 156,124,92,89,78,67,56,47 (desc by upvotes), thread-2(89) ranked below thread-7(92). Cast 4 upvotes on thread-2 via separate accounts, raising it to 93; trending list re-sorted with thread-2 now ranked above thread-7 (93>92), full list remained descending.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Thread reply total went 0 replies -> 'Replies (1)' heading with 1 listed reply -> after second reply, thread.reply-count='2 replies' matching 2 listed replies each time.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No recent time window is stated or applied for Trending/Most Active views\", \"actual\": \"Trending Discussions and Most Active Discussions headings only show the generic subtitle 'Join the conversation with our community' with no mention of a time window (e.g. 'last 7 days', 'this week'). The ranked threads themselves are all timestamped 'over 2 years ago', showing the lists rank by all-time upvote/reply totals rather than interactions within any stated recent period.\", \"evidence\": \"Trending/Most Active page header subtitle: 'Join the conversation with our community' (no time window text). All 8 listed threads show time='over 2 years ago'.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Community stats and category counts are static and do not update when new discussions, replies, or members are created\", \"actual\": \"Registered a new account (ct21tester) - stats.members remained 892 (no increment). Created a new thread in General Discussion - stats.threads remained '1,